sombra (0.2.0) unstable; urgency=medium

  * The daemon is driven over the system bus instead of a unix socket, on
    io.github.svesh87.Sombra. Who may drive it is a bus policy file and one
    polkit action with allow_active=yes, so the person at this screen is
    allowed without being asked anything.
  * The group sombra is no longer needed and no longer created. Nobody has to
    join anything or log back in to use the console. An installation that has
    the group can keep it; it grants nothing.
  * The --socket option became --bus-address on sombrad, sombra and
    sombra-tray.
  * The console no longer polls: it reads what the daemon publishes and is told
    what changes.
  * The depth of the telemetry ring can be changed with the arrows of its field
    again.
  * The console's window and its entry in a dock now carry the application's
    own icon.

 -- Sergei Sveshnikov <sergei@svesh.dev>  Wed, 12 Aug 2026 00:33:59 +0200

